# FinTrack frontend. Browser code needs no API URL: it always calls relative /api/...
# paths on its own origin, which keeps the HttpOnly refresh cookie first-party.
#
# Local development: nothing is required. The Vite dev server proxies /api to
# http://localhost:8080 (see devProxy.ts). To point it at another local backend, set
# this before `npm run dev` (server-only; never exposed to the browser):
# DEV_API_PROXY_TARGET=http://localhost:8080
#
# Vercel (server-side function api/proxy.ts), set per environment in the Vercel
# project, not in this file:
#   BACKEND_ORIGIN=https://your-backend.example.com
# - Server-only: never prefix it with VITE_, or it would be bundled into the browser.
# - An origin only: https, no trailing slash-path, no /api suffix, no credentials.
# - Preview, staging, and production each point at their own backend.
#
# Obsolete: VITE_API_BASE_URL is no longer read. Remove it from .env files and from
# Vercel; direct cross-origin calls are not the supported refresh-cookie topology.
